WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.740
[upbeat music]

2
00:00:02.880 --> 00:00:06.110
Standardized integration workflows
are key to ensuring chiplets

3
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:09.770
from different vendors can be seamlessly
integrated into a single system.

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:14.080
Chiplet integration requires
a structured process to manage design,

5
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:17.060
verification, packaging, and testing.

6
00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:21.540
Without standardization, interoperability
becomes a major challenge.

7
00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.300
The chiplet product development workflow
is typically divided into four phases:

8
00:00:26.780 --> 00:00:29.660
planning and prototyping,
design implementation,

9
00:00:29.940 --> 00:00:33.100
verification and signoff,
and final manufacturing.

10
00:00:33.660 --> 00:00:37.830
In the planning phase, engineers
define system architecture and ensure

11
00:00:37.840 --> 00:00:42.160
compatibility between chiplets,
packaging, and interconnect standards.

12
00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:48.310
Next, during the design implementation
phase, chip designers design

13
00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.340
chiplets according to the specifications
outlined in the planning phase.

14
00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:54.960
For existing chiplets from other vendors,

15
00:00:55.180 --> 00:00:59.300
they can use standardized data
exchange formats such as JEDEC JESD30

16
00:00:59.740 --> 00:01:03.960
or CDXML to ensure consistency
across tools and vendors.

17
00:01:04.900 --> 00:01:08.240
Power, signal integrity,
and thermal models are

18
00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:11.900
critical for ensuring chiplets
function correctly within the package.

19
00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.900
Standardized formats help
simplify integration and analysis.

20
00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:18.330
The verification and signoff phase

21
00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:22.200
ensures all components meet
performance and reliability standards.

22
00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:26.600
This includes functional simulation,
die-to-die signal verification,

23
00:01:26.660 --> 00:01:29.820
and compliance testing.
During manufacturing,

24
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.760
chiplets are tested at multiple levels
from wafer level to system level.

25
00:01:35.380 --> 00:01:39.210
Interoperability standards
like UCIe and Bunch of Wires,

26
00:01:39.220 --> 00:01:42.280
or BoW, define how chiplets communicate,

27
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.660
making it possible for components from
different vendors to work together.

28
00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.860
A well-defined integration
workflow ensures higher efficiency,

29
00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:56.780
reduced development time, and greater
market adoption for chiplet-based designs.

30
00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:01.830
In this course, we explored the critical
aspects of integration workflow standards,

31
00:02:02.120 --> 00:02:04.140
including data exchange formats,

32
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:07.180
verification processes,
and best practices.

33
00:02:07.220 --> 00:02:12.680
[upbeat music]

